        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/h/y/laugharne-wp/bank-between-fields-with-harts.jpg",
          "filename": "Bank between fields, with harts-tongue ferns, Laugharne - geograph.org.uk - 578564.jpg",
          "caption": "Bank between fields, with harts-tongue ferns, Laugharne Inside the area protected by the sea wall the land is divided by banks.  This one is supposed to have a public footpath along the top, but it is blocked by impenetrable thickets of thorn bushes. The innocent-looking ditch is actually deep water about 2m wide, partly hidden by the plants growing in it.  On the Explorer map, it seems that the public footpath might be along the edge of the field behind the fence, but this seems unlikely as there is no stile into the field and there are MOD signs on the fence.",
          "alt": "Bank between fields, with harts-tongue ferns, Laugharne Inside the area protected by the sea wall the land is divided by banks.  This one is supposed to have a public footpath along the top, but it is blocked by impenetrable thickets of thorn bushes. The innocent-looking ditch is actually deep water about 2m wide, partly hidden by the plants growing in it.  On the Explorer map, it seems that the public footpath might be along the edge of the field behind the fence, but this seems unlikely as there is no stile into the field and there are MOD signs on the fence.",
          "width": 640,
